# Tracer: rational and natural arithmetic closure
#
# Before (Litex verified, but compiler emission stopped):
# forall a, b Q:
#     a * b $in Q
# Former compiler behavior: the verifier kept only a generic builtin-rule
# label, so the compiler had no exact rational-closure certificate to replay.
#
# Now: rational `+`, `-`, `*`, `/` and natural `+`, `*` replay exact
# verifier-selected closure certificates through proved native-carrier rules.
# Source binders stay complex-valued and retain independent Litex.In evidence.
forall a, b Q:
    a + b $in Q

forall a, b Q:
    a - b $in Q

forall a, b Q:
    a * b $in Q

forall a, b Q:
    b != 0
    =>:
        a / b $in Q

forall a, b N:
    a + b $in N

forall a, b N:
    a * b $in N

# Boundary (Litex verifies; compiler remains fail-closed):
# forall a Q, z Z:
#     a != 0
#     =>:
#         a^z $in Q
# Rational power has verifier closure evidence, but the current compiler has no
# reviewed native power term/evidence adapter. This batch must not invent one.
#
# Evidence:
# target/release/litex -compact -strict -runner -f lean/examples/18_RationalNaturalClosures.lit
# cargo test --release --test litex_to_lean_compiler_tracers rational_and_natural_carrier_closures
# cd lean && ./compiler.sh check examples
